        "message": "LU-16127 tests: check OSD cache stats in sanity 255b\n\nsanity test_255b measured Cached in /proc/meminfo on the OSS\nright after dropping all caches. Other processes on the OSS\nrefill the page cache in that window, so the release measured\nafter dontneed can fall below the threshold even though every\npage of the file was dropped.\n\nCount the OST0000 OSD cache hits and misses around each\nwillread instead: a second willread must hit the cache, and a\nwillread after dontneed must miss it. Skip parallel runs so\nother test I/O cannot mask missing hits or misses. This no\nlonger drops caches on the OSS.\n\nFixes: a5a7890093ea (\"LU-4931 ladvise: Add dontneed advice support for ladvise\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=255b,ONLY_REPEAT=50\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iadda22ca15ebb3a5e161609ddfefeb9e6db1f756\n"
      },
